  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2022-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Rearranging, \\(y^4 - 2y^2 + 1 = x^4,\\) so \\((y^2 - 1)^2 = (x^2)^2.\\) This factors as \\[ (y^2 - 1 - x^2)(y^2 - 1 + x^2) = 0. \\]\n\nThus either \\(y^2 - x^2 = 1,\\) which is a hyperbola, or \\(x^2 + y^2 = 1,\\) which is a circle.\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Move everything to one side to get \\((y^2 - 1)^2 = (x^2)^2\\)",
        "Factor as a difference of squares, giving two separate equations"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
